.TH EUCLID-CLI-ETS-STOP-SERVER 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ets-stop-server \- ask the manager to stop a transfer server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ets stop-server
.BR \-\-server\-id | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Marks a transfer server as one that should not be running.
.PP
As with
.BR euclid-cli-ets-start-server (1),
the command records the intent and returns; the Euclid manager stops the
.BR euclid-ftp (8)
or
.BR euclid-sftp (8)
process on its next reconcile pass, a few seconds later. Clients
connected at that moment are disconnected.
.PP
The definition is kept, so the server can be started again later with
the same settings - this is the difference from
.BR euclid-cli-ets-delete-server (1),
which removes the definition entirely. Stopping is also what
.BR euclid-cli-ets-update-server (1)
pairs with to apply a changed setting to a running server.
.PP
Nothing in the bucket is affected. Objects uploaded through this server
remain, and stay reachable through
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
or any other transfer server pointed at the same bucket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-server\-id " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the server to stop. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The desired state was recorded; the server's definition is printed as
JSON with \fIdesiredState\fR \fISTOPPED\fR. This does
.I not
mean the process has exited yet.
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, the caller is not an authenticated
administrator, the server could not be reached, or no server has that ID
(HTTP 404).
.SH EXAMPLES
Stop a server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets stop-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Apply a changed setting to a running server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets update-server \e
    --server-id sftp1 --port 2223
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets stop-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets start-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-start-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-update-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-delete-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-list-servers (1)
